{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["occ"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"text":"@property","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"nonatomic","kind":"keyword"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"copy","kind":"keyword"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SCDetailModelSectionAction_Block","identifier":"doc:\/\/ie.dgapps.STV\/documentation\/STV\/SCDetailModelSectionAction_Block","preciseIdentifier":"c:SCSectionActions.h@T@SCDetailModelSectionAction_Block","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"detailModelCreated","kind":"identifier"},{"text":";","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This action is typically used to initially configure the detail model (like set a custom tag for example). Most of the model’s settings can also be configure in the detailModelConfigured action.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Example:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"objective-c","code":["\/\/ Objective-C","sectionActions.detailModelCreated = ^(SCTableViewSection *section, SCTableViewModel *detailModel, NSIndexPath *indexPath)","{","    detailModel.tag = 100;","};"]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This action is only applicable to sections that generate detail views, such as SCArrayOfObjectsSection."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"warning","name":"Warning","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the case where the detail model is not associated with an existing row (such as the case when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SCArrayOfObjectsSection"},{"type":"text","text":" creates a new item), indexPath.row will be set to NSNotFound. This is a good way to test if the detail model was generated for a new item or an al